            "Figure 2 captions the Anderson curve as K0=236(1) GPa, while the abstract, Results prose, and Table 3 report 237(1) GPa. The repeated prose/table value is stored; the caption-only value is not added as a duplicate EOS.",
            "Results prose says Z=2, whereas the Table 1 note explicitly says Cmcm Z=4 and the listed conventional-cell sites have multiplicities 4, 4, 4, and 8. Peritheos uses the conventional Cmcm cell and Z=4; Z=2 is consistent only with a primitive-cell count.",
            "Table 2 prints MgSiO3 a=2.250(3) A in row 3, inconsistent with b, c, and V=120.11(22) A^3; a near 2.450 A would be required. The printed 2.250 value is preserved, and EOS reproduction uses the independently printed volume."
          ],
          "unresolved_issues": [
            "The article does not state the confidence convention of the parenthetical K0 errors and publishes no parameter covariance matrix.",
            "The exact weighted-least-squares objective and weights used by the cited Angel (2000) program are not printed.",
            "The fixed 162.86 A^3 zero-pressure volume was adopted from a 0 K LDA calculation even though the experimental isotherm and reported K0 are at 300 K."
          ]
        },
        "parameter_provenance": {
          "determination_method": "Measurements or their experimental reduction determine this EOS; source: Abstract; Experimental methods; Results and printed EOS equation; Tables 1-3; Figure 2 and caption.",
          "equation": "Journal page 476: the printed third-order Birch-Murnaghan equation uses x=(V/V0)^(1/3), with P=(3/2)K0(x^-7-x^-5)[1+(3/4)(K0_prime-4)(x^-2-1)]. Fixing K0_prime=4 makes the executable curve exactly BM2.",
          "V0": "Journal page 477 and Table 3: 162.86 A^3, fixed; adopted from the 0 K LDA calculation of Oganov and Ono (2004), not measured at ambient pressure.",
          "K0": "Results prose and Table 3, journal page 477: 237(1) GPa for pressures reduced with the Anderson et al. (1989) gold standard.",
          "K0_prime": "Results prose and Table 3, journal page 477: fixed at 4; represented implicitly by BM2 rather than as a fitted parameter.",
          "reference_state": "The fit is described as a 300 K isothermal EOS with a zero-pressure V0 and K0, extrapolated from 116.1-144.4 GPa data. V0 itself was adopted from a 0 K LDA calculation.",
          "fit_selection_and_weighting": "Experimental methods and Results: all six Table 2 P-V observations were used in a weighted least-squares fit with the method cited to Angel (2000); the article does not publish the exact objective or covariance matrix.",
